  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NCC BC-CIJV&amp;PCJV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The focus of this proposal is to deliver a clear benefit to the conservation of wetlands and associated uplands, which provide critical habitat for waterfowl, shorebirds, waterbirds and wetland-associated land birds within the PCJV and the CIJV in British Columbia. Partners will perpetually protect 15 acres (consisting of 2 wetland acres and 13 upland acres), and enhance 78acres (consisting of 36 acres of wetlands and 42 acres of uplands). Management activities will be undertaken on 4,839 acres which are protected as part of this and/or previous NAWCA projects.</narrative>
  </description>
